WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.468 --> 00:00:03.836
-The President said in an
interview if he had the chance

00:00:03.836 --> 00:00:05.671
to collude with
a foreign government in 2020,

00:00:05.671 --> 00:00:06.873
he would do it.

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:09.208
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:09.208 --> 00:00:14.080
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.849
You'd be forgiven for thinking
Donald Trump doesn't actually

00:00:16.849 --> 00:00:19.418
do that much work as president,
but you'd be wrong.

00:00:19.418 --> 00:00:21.221
He's got a very important job,

00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:23.856
as we learned today
from an interview on ABC.

00:00:23.856 --> 00:00:26.058
Trump is in charge
of picking new paint colors

00:00:26.058 --> 00:00:28.094
for Air Force One.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:29.729
And he is very proud of that.

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:31.164
-George, take a look at this.

00:00:31.164 --> 00:00:33.533
-Then, at the White House,
a surprise from the President --

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:36.035
the first look
at an updated aircraft,

00:00:36.035 --> 00:00:39.405
a new look for Air Force One
that he designed himself.

00:00:39.405 --> 00:00:42.308
-There's your new Air Force One.

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:44.777
And I'm doing that for other
presidents, not for me.

00:00:44.777 --> 00:00:47.213
-It's scheduled
to arrive in 2024,

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:49.215
the exterior getting a makeover,

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:51.417
with a new red, white, and blue
paint scheme,

00:00:51.417 --> 00:00:53.919
a departure from the iconic
blue and white.

00:00:53.919 --> 00:00:55.521
-We had different choices here.

00:00:55.521 --> 00:00:57.623
These are all
slightly different.

00:00:57.623 --> 00:00:58.858
-All right. I think
I know what happened here.

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:00.626
Trump's staff
just gave him a menu

00:01:00.626 --> 00:01:02.395
with a bunch of airplanes on it
to keep him busy

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:04.596
while they run the government.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.596 --> 00:01:06.733
You know, like how you give
a child at a restaurant

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:09.468
a placemat with a maze on it.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.468 --> 00:01:11.671
You know, if you zoom in
on that image Trump is holding,

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:13.639
at the top, it says,
"Spot the difference."

00:01:13.639 --> 00:01:17.777
[ Laughter and applause ]
This right here --

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:22.648
This right here is the only part
of the job Trump loves --

00:01:22.648 --> 00:01:25.885
feeling important, basking
in the trapping of the office.

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:27.486
In that same interview,
for example,

00:01:27.486 --> 00:01:29.322
he and George Stephanopoulos
took a ride

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:31.757
in the presidential limo,
where Trump denied reports

00:01:31.757 --> 00:01:35.028
that his own internal polls
show him trailing in key states.

00:01:35.028 --> 00:01:36.729
-I asked the President
about those reports

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:38.631
that he's trailing Biden
in the polls.

00:01:38.631 --> 00:01:40.266
-Well, I don't believe
those polls.

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:42.134
There's no way
he beats me in Texas.

00:01:42.134 --> 00:01:43.303
-But even your own polls

00:01:43.303 --> 00:01:44.737
show you're behind right now,
don't they?

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:47.740
-No, my polls show
that I'm winning everywhere.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.709
I don't know.
-We've all seen these reports

00:01:49.709 --> 00:01:52.445
that in 15 out of 17 states,
you spend $2 million on a poll,

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:54.647
and you're behind
in 15 of 17 states.

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:56.149
-Nobody showed you those polls

00:01:56.149 --> 00:01:58.350
because those polls don't exist,
George.

00:01:58.350 --> 00:01:59.985
Those polls don't exist.

00:01:59.985 --> 00:02:02.822
-Oh, great. He's back
to his [bleep] Jedi routine.

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:04.557
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:07.659
Also, why are they
so close together?

00:02:07.659 --> 00:02:14.734
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:19.272
Is this the presidential limo
or an Uber Pool?

00:02:19.272 --> 00:02:21.173
"We're picking up
two more people.

00:02:21.173 --> 00:02:23.643
Can you guys kind of squinch
together back there?"

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:25.444
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.444 --> 00:02:27.947
Later in the Oval Office,
Trump was asked why he insists

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:30.416
on lying so brazenly
and so obsessively

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:31.784
about his poll numbers,
and he offered

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:33.519
an interesting self-assessment.

00:02:33.519 --> 00:02:38.724
-Why does it bother you so much?
-Because it's untrue.

00:02:38.724 --> 00:02:39.892
I like the truth.

00:02:39.892 --> 00:02:41.727
You know, I'm actually
a very honest guy.

00:02:41.727 --> 00:02:42.828
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.828 --> 00:02:44.730
And even that statement
wasn't honest.

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:46.599
When you say, "I'm actually
a very honest guy,

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:49.735
that's the classic tell that
you're not an honest guy.

00:02:49.735 --> 00:02:51.904
Nobody who's honest
says they're honest.

00:02:51.904 --> 00:02:54.707
The only people who claim
to be honest are car dealers,

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:56.108
personal injury lawyers.

00:02:56.108 --> 00:02:58.911
You never hear someone say,
"Our charity builds houses

00:02:58.911 --> 00:03:01.314
for the homeless
the honest way."

00:03:01.314 --> 00:03:02.615
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.615 --> 00:03:04.417
Trump just says this stuff
and thinks we'll buy it

00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:06.753
despite the fact
that we now have over 400 pages

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:09.522
of definitive proof that he
is not, in fact, an honest guy

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:12.158
in the form of Special Counsel
Robert Mueller's final report.

00:03:12.158 --> 00:03:15.261
And yet he just continues on
because he has no shame.

00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:16.929
We're so used
to Trump's corruption now

00:03:16.929 --> 00:03:18.497
that we could ask him
what he did today,

00:03:18.497 --> 00:03:20.166
and he'd go,
"Oh, I had breakfast,

00:03:20.166 --> 00:03:22.134
played a round of gold,
I shot a guy,

00:03:22.134 --> 00:03:23.836
and then I saw the new
"Secret Life of Pets,"

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:25.938
and we'd say,
"Oh, is that any good?"

00:03:25.938 --> 00:03:28.074
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.074 --> 00:03:29.375
And that's what he did
last night

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:31.177
during the same interview on ABC

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:32.311
when he just
straight up admitted

00:03:32.311 --> 00:03:33.546
that if he had the opportunity

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:35.848
to collude with a foreign
government again in 2020,

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:37.283
he would definitely do it.

00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:40.185
-Your campaign this time around,
if foreigners -- if Russia,

00:03:40.185 --> 00:03:41.454
if China, if someone else,

00:03:41.454 --> 00:03:42.755
offers you information
on an opponent,

00:03:42.755 --> 00:03:45.458
should they accept it
or should they call the FBI?

00:03:45.458 --> 00:03:47.159
-I think maybe you do both.

00:03:47.159 --> 00:03:48.727
I think you might
want to listen.

00:03:48.727 --> 00:03:50.729
I don't think there's
anything wrong with listening.

00:03:50.729 --> 00:03:55.234
If somebody called
from a country -- Norway --

00:03:55.234 --> 00:03:57.469
"We have information
on your opponent."

00:03:57.469 --> 00:03:59.171
"Oh." I think
I'd want to hear it.

00:03:59.171 --> 00:04:01.240
-You want that kind of
interference in our elections?

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:03.209
-It's not an interference.
They have information.

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:04.577
I think I'd take it.

00:04:04.577 --> 00:04:06.078
-There it is.
He just said it.

00:04:06.078 --> 00:04:09.782
The guy who has spent two years
scream tweeting "No collusion"

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:13.019
is now saying, "If anyone's
down the collude, I'm your guy."

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:14.453
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.453 --> 00:04:15.988
This guy has no shame.

00:04:15.988 --> 00:04:18.157
If Trump had been President
during Watergate,

00:04:18.157 --> 00:04:21.027
he would've left a business card
at the break-in.

00:04:21.027 --> 00:04:22.495
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.495 --> 00:04:25.030
We have all this evidence
that Russia reached out to Trump

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:27.233
to collude, and now we have
Trump himself on the record

00:04:27.233 --> 00:04:28.901
saying, "If Russia reached out
to me to collude,

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:30.369
I would do it."

00:04:30.369 --> 00:04:32.772
Normally, to get someone to say
they'd commit a crime like that,

00:04:32.772 --> 00:04:34.440
you have to haul them down
to the precinct

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:36.008
and play good cop/bad cop.

00:04:36.008 --> 00:04:38.577
Trump's episode of "Law &amp; Order"
would be about six minutes long.

00:04:38.577 --> 00:04:40.512
Brisco and Green would walk
into his office,

00:04:40.512 --> 00:04:43.449
and he'd go, "What's up, guys?
You find that hooker I killed?"

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:46.586
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.586 --> 00:04:51.657
Seriously, why --
[ Applause ]

00:04:51.657 --> 00:04:54.159
Why are we not just treating
this as a confession?

00:04:54.159 --> 00:04:56.228
Just because he's phrasing it
as hypothetical

00:04:56.228 --> 00:04:57.996
doesn't make it
any less damning.

00:04:57.996 --> 00:05:00.266
If your co-worker at Burger King
turned to you and said,

00:05:00.266 --> 00:05:01.967
"You know, I'm not saying
I ever done it,

00:05:01.967 --> 00:05:04.070
but if someone dared me
to coat my balls in batter

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:07.406
and dip them in the deep-fryer,
I'd definitely consider it."

00:05:07.406 --> 00:05:09.075
[ Laughter ]

00:05:09.075 --> 00:05:10.609
You'd call your boss and say,

00:05:10.609 --> 00:05:13.279
"I think that we need
to replace the deep-fryer."

00:05:13.279 --> 00:05:14.813
[ Laughter ]

00:05:14.813 --> 00:05:16.849
After that interview aired,
there was an uproar from,

00:05:16.849 --> 00:05:18.450
you know, sane people
who think the President

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:19.919
shouldn't go on TV
and tell people

00:05:19.919 --> 00:05:21.220
he's down to commit a crime.

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:23.188
Democrats renewed their calls
for impeachment,

00:05:23.188 --> 00:05:24.990
so Trump hopped on Twitter
to defend himself

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:27.559
with a dumb argument
that was topped in its dumbness

00:05:27.559 --> 00:05:30.096
only by a truly
mind-bending typo.

00:05:30.096 --> 00:05:32.665
-He says, "I meet and talk to
foreign governments every day.

00:05:32.665 --> 00:05:34.333
I just met with
the Queen of England, U.K.,

00:05:34.333 --> 00:05:36.702
the Prince of Whales,"
which he spells wrong.

00:05:36.702 --> 00:05:40.206
-Yep.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.206 --> 00:05:42.741
He spelled it
like the marine mammal,

00:05:42.741 --> 00:05:44.577
not like the country of Wales.

00:05:44.577 --> 00:05:45.778
[ Laughter ]

00:05:45.778 --> 00:05:47.246
He literally just met the guy.

00:05:47.246 --> 00:05:48.747
Trump must have been
so disappointed.

00:05:48.747 --> 00:05:51.583
"You're not a whale."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:51.583 --> 00:05:52.818
"Where's your blow hole?"

00:05:52.818 --> 00:05:55.221
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:55.221 --> 00:05:56.723
And then,
with that out of the way,

00:05:56.723 --> 00:05:58.891
he continued with
his very stupid argument.

00:05:58.891 --> 00:06:00.559
-"The P.M. of
the United Kingdom,

00:06:00.559 --> 00:06:02.695
the P.M. of Ireland,
the president of France,

00:06:02.695 --> 00:06:05.431
and the president of Poland.
We talked about everything.

00:06:05.431 --> 00:06:07.166
Should I immediately
call the FBI

00:06:07.166 --> 00:06:08.801
about these calls and meetings?

00:06:08.801 --> 00:06:11.270
How ridiculous.
I would never be trusted again."

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:13.439
-No one's arguing you should
call the FBI after meeting

00:06:13.439 --> 00:06:15.574
with the foreign leaders
as part of your actual job,

00:06:15.574 --> 00:06:18.878
unless one of those leaders
does or offer something illegal.

00:06:18.878 --> 00:06:20.346
And even then,
it depends what it is.

00:06:20.346 --> 00:06:22.081
If you meet with Putin,
he says,

00:06:22.081 --> 00:06:23.382
"We hacked
your opponent's e-mails

00:06:23.382 --> 00:06:24.883
and stole private information,"
then, yes,

00:06:24.883 --> 00:06:26.185
you should call the FBI.

00:06:26.185 --> 00:06:27.954
If you meet with the
Queen of England and she says,

00:06:27.954 --> 00:06:29.321
"Want to take
a rip off this bong?"

00:06:29.321 --> 00:06:31.224
I'd say play it cool.
Don't dime on her, man!

00:06:31.224 --> 00:06:32.491
[ Laughter ]

00:06:32.491 --> 00:06:35.461
Don't dime on the Queen.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:35.461 --> 00:06:37.229
But the most important thing
to remember here is,

00:06:37.229 --> 00:06:39.332
this is not
a random hypothetical.

00:06:39.332 --> 00:06:42.000
Trump is actively inviting
Russia or China

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:43.869
or any other foreign government,
for that matter,

00:06:43.869 --> 00:06:46.672
to actively intervene in
the 2020 election on his behalf,

00:06:46.672 --> 00:06:48.607
and we know this because,
in 2016,

00:06:48.607 --> 00:06:51.577
Russia's military intelligence
agency, known as the GRU,

00:06:51.577 --> 00:06:53.746
basically took directions
from Trump.

00:06:53.746 --> 00:06:55.147
Remember when Trump said this?

00:06:55.147 --> 00:06:59.385
-Russia, if you're listening,
I hope you're able to find

00:06:59.385 --> 00:07:03.756
the 30,000 e-mails
that are missing.

00:07:03.756 --> 00:07:08.260
I think you will probably be
rewarded mightily by our press.

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:09.795
-Well, according
to the Mueller report,

00:07:09.795 --> 00:07:11.898
"Within approximately
five hours of Trump's statement,

00:07:11.898 --> 00:07:14.400
GRU officers targeted,
for the first time,

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:15.868
Clinton's personal office."

00:07:15.868 --> 00:07:17.803
So it turns out
they were listening.

00:07:17.803 --> 00:07:19.705
In fact, at this point,
I think the Russians

00:07:19.705 --> 00:07:22.074
are the only ones who haven't
tuned out Donald Trump.

00:07:22.074 --> 00:07:24.710
The rest of us just ignore it,
and when we walk by a TV

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:26.411
and see Trump
on the White House lawn

00:07:26.411 --> 00:07:28.380
next to the helicopter,
shouting at reporters,

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:31.083
red-faced, doing that
weird thing where he draws a box

00:07:31.083 --> 00:07:33.886
with his hands for no reason,
waving around a random

00:07:33.886 --> 00:07:36.222
piece of paper he pulled
out of his coat pocket

00:07:36.222 --> 00:07:38.991
like he just got some positive
test results back.

00:07:38.991 --> 00:07:42.427
"Good news -- the doctors say
it hasn't spread to my brain.

00:07:42.427 --> 00:07:46.098
They say it comes
from my brain."

00:07:46.098 --> 00:07:48.701
So we know that the Russians
have already reacted

00:07:48.701 --> 00:07:51.703
to an invitation from Trump
to interfere in the election.

00:07:51.703 --> 00:07:53.638
That's what makes Trump's latest
comments so crazy.

00:07:53.638 --> 00:07:54.840
It's not hypothetical.

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:56.876
He knows they will try
to help him again,

00:07:56.876 --> 00:07:59.011
and he's signaling to them
that he'd welcome it.

00:07:59.011 --> 00:08:01.613
In fact, in that same interview,
Trump actually mocked the idea

00:08:01.613 --> 00:08:03.582
that he should call the FBI
if a foreign government

00:08:03.582 --> 00:08:05.985
attempted to interfere
in an election on his behalf.

00:08:05.985 --> 00:08:08.120
-Okay. Let's put yourself
in a position.

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:10.422
You're a congressman.
Somebody comes up and says,

00:08:10.422 --> 00:08:13.025
"Hey, I have information
on your opponent."

00:08:13.025 --> 00:08:14.360
Do you call the FBI?

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:15.761
-If it's coming from Russia,
you do.

00:08:15.761 --> 00:08:17.295
-I've seen a lot of things
over my life.

00:08:17.295 --> 00:08:19.998
I don't think in my whole life
I've ever called the FBI.

00:08:19.998 --> 00:08:22.334
-Oh, really?
Oh, really?

00:08:22.334 --> 00:08:23.769
You haven't?
Because I'm shocked to hear

00:08:23.769 --> 00:08:26.305
that the famously corrupt
New York real-estate mogul

00:08:26.305 --> 00:08:28.907
who owned Atlantic City casinos,
doesn't pay his taxes,

00:08:28.907 --> 00:08:30.343
has been sued
thousands of times,

00:08:30.343 --> 00:08:32.678
and paid hush money to cover up
an affair with a porn star

00:08:32.678 --> 00:08:34.446
doesn't have
a great relationship

00:08:34.446 --> 00:08:36.181
with law enforcement.

00:08:36.181 --> 00:08:39.451
I just assume the only contact
Trump has ever had with the FBI

00:08:39.451 --> 00:08:42.855
are anonymous faxes with letters
cut out from magazines.

00:08:42.855 --> 00:08:44.390
[ Laughter ]

00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:45.491
Although,
who are we kidding?

00:08:45.491 --> 00:08:47.426
He would still
definitely sign it.

00:08:47.426 --> 00:08:49.195
[ Laughter ]

00:08:49.195 --> 00:08:51.096
But in many ways,
this moment was inevitable.

00:08:51.096 --> 00:08:53.666
Trump and his aides have
been foreshadowing for months

00:08:53.666 --> 00:08:54.967
that this was coming,
that they didn't think

00:08:54.967 --> 00:08:57.336
collusion was a crime,
and if they had the chance,

00:08:57.336 --> 00:08:58.704
they would do it again.

00:08:58.704 --> 00:09:00.405
Earlier this month,
Trump's son-in-law,

00:09:00.405 --> 00:09:02.875
Jared Kushner, said in
an interview that if he received

00:09:02.875 --> 00:09:05.177
another e-mail from a foreign
government offering dirt

00:09:05.177 --> 00:09:07.847
on a political opponent,
like he did in 2016,

00:09:07.847 --> 00:09:09.949
he wasn't sure
he would call the FBI.

00:09:09.949 --> 00:09:13.285
-On June the 8th, 2016,
you were sent an e-mail

00:09:13.285 --> 00:09:15.788
with an offer of help for the
Trump campaign

00:09:15.788 --> 00:09:17.089
from the Russian government.

00:09:17.089 --> 00:09:19.325
Why didn't you pick up
the phoned and call the FBI?

00:09:19.325 --> 00:09:21.293
It was an e-mail
that said Russia --

00:09:21.293 --> 00:09:23.529
that said the Russian government
was trying to help.

00:09:23.529 --> 00:09:24.930
Look, why didn't you do that?

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:26.999
-The e-mail that I got on
my iPhone at the time

00:09:26.999 --> 00:09:28.600
basically said,
"Show up at 4:00."

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:30.870
I didn't scroll down.
I never would have thought --

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:32.671
-It had "Russia"
in the subject line.

00:09:32.671 --> 00:09:35.007
-Again, I would get about
250 e-mails a day,

00:09:35.007 --> 00:09:36.942
and so I literally saw
"Show up at 4:00,"

00:09:36.942 --> 00:09:38.343
I showed up at 4:00.

00:09:38.343 --> 00:09:40.145
-Would you call the FBI
if it happened again?

00:09:40.145 --> 00:09:41.981
-I don't know.
It's hard to do hypotheticals,

00:09:41.981 --> 00:09:43.916
but the reality is
is that we were not

00:09:43.916 --> 00:09:45.784
given anything
that was salacious.

00:09:45.784 --> 00:09:47.919
-Okay. First of all,
the subject line of the e-mail

00:09:47.919 --> 00:09:50.255
was literally
"Forward, Russia, Clinton,

00:09:50.255 --> 00:09:51.790
private and confidential."

00:09:51.790 --> 00:09:53.659
I don't care
how many e-mails you get a day.

00:09:53.659 --> 00:09:54.960
That subject line sticks out.

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:56.562
It doesn't matter
who it's from.

00:09:56.562 --> 00:09:58.297
If I see an e-mail that says
"Pottery Barn,

00:09:58.297 --> 00:09:59.899
private and confidential,"
I'd be like,

00:09:59.899 --> 00:10:02.201
"Ooh! What's your secret,
Pottery Barn?"

00:10:02.201 --> 00:10:04.770
[ Laughter ]

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:05.971
Trump aides
have basically been saying

00:10:05.971 --> 00:10:07.172
a version of this for months.

00:10:07.172 --> 00:10:08.741
Just last month,
his personal lawyer

00:10:08.741 --> 00:10:12.310
and private vampire,
Rudy Giuliani, went on TV

00:10:12.310 --> 00:10:14.580
and bragged about a bizarre plan
he had concocted

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:16.148
to go to Ukraine and dig up dirt

00:10:16.148 --> 00:10:18.050
on the Russia investigation
and Joe Biden,

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:19.985
and he actually said
in an interview

00:10:19.985 --> 00:10:23.188
that if he wanted to mettle
in the 2020 election, he could.

00:10:23.188 --> 00:10:25.957
-President Trump's
personal attorney Rudy Giuliani

00:10:25.957 --> 00:10:28.427
planning to travel
to Ukraine soon.

00:10:28.427 --> 00:10:31.030
"The New York Times" reports
he will ask that country's

00:10:31.030 --> 00:10:33.198
new president
to investigate the origin

00:10:33.198 --> 00:10:35.867
of Special Counsel Mueller's
Russian investigation.

00:10:35.867 --> 00:10:38.337
Giuliani will also press Ukraine
to look into

00:10:38.337 --> 00:10:40.973
Joe Biden's son's involvement

00:10:40.973 --> 00:10:44.844
in a gas company owned by
a Ukrainian oligarch.

00:10:44.844 --> 00:10:47.847
-The election of 2020
is a long time from now.

00:10:47.847 --> 00:10:50.449
And if I wanted to meddle in
that election, which I don't,

00:10:50.449 --> 00:10:52.218
I could've held this for a year

00:10:52.218 --> 00:10:54.887
and dropped it
right before the convention.

00:10:54.887 --> 00:10:56.121
-Speaking of meddling,
I got to ask,

00:10:56.121 --> 00:10:57.723
who's meddling with your hair,

00:10:57.723 --> 00:11:01.327
because this is what Rudy's hair
normally looks like.

00:11:01.327 --> 00:11:04.897
You really think the spray-on
hair is making you look younger?

00:11:04.897 --> 00:11:06.832
You look like the guy
who gives you

00:11:06.832 --> 00:11:09.468
your next assignment
in "Grand Theft Auto."

00:11:09.468 --> 00:11:11.103
[ Laughter ]

00:11:11.103 --> 00:11:13.939
"You got to go to the police,
Dmitri."

00:11:13.939 --> 00:11:18.310
[ Laughter ]

00:11:18.310 --> 00:11:20.880
Trump and the people around him
are actively inviting

00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:24.015
the interference of a foreign
government in the 2020 campaign.

00:11:24.015 --> 00:11:25.417
The only answer
to that is impeachment.

00:11:25.417 --> 00:11:27.386
Democrats need to lay out
all the evidence

00:11:27.386 --> 00:11:29.922
of Trump's corruption
in a high-profile, public forum

00:11:29.922 --> 00:11:32.090
for voters to see,
and when asked why,

00:11:32.090 --> 00:11:33.626
they should quote Trump
and say...

00:11:33.626 --> 00:11:35.060
-I like the truth.

00:11:35.060 --> 00:11:36.428
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:11:36.428 --> 00:11:40.266
[ Cheers and applause ]

